WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:57.233
[Music]

00:00:57.233 --> 00:01:06.066
[Narrator:] A mother always wonders when her child comes home in tears.

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:07.399
What's this?

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.480
Kaye's swimsuit?

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:15.333
Now that's a reaction.

00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:20.433
Tears help sometimes.

00:01:20.433 --> 00:01:23.866
For Kaye today, it's a real tragedy.

00:01:23.866 --> 00:01:27.466
She'd set her heart on making the high school swim team.

00:01:27.466 --> 00:01:32.706
Trouble is, she tires so quickly these days.

00:01:34.433 --> 00:01:38.566
Even the coach sees it.

00:01:38.566 --> 00:01:43.332
It's hard to take that kind of disappointment when you're just 15.

00:01:43.333 --> 00:01:44.999
Eddie Roberts.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:51.866
She knows she'll never get to know him if she doesn't make the team.

00:01:51.866 --> 00:01:58.132
Too bad Kaye, but that's the way it is, and even mother-love can't change it.

00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:04.033
[Music]

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:05.599
Your family...

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:10.700
Well Kaye, the women just don't have the strength for sports and swimming.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:21.700
[Music]

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:26.166
What, Kaye? You don't think anyone should have to feel this way?

00:02:26.166 --> 00:02:33.746
You're going to see a doctor? Kaye, that school nurse is talking nonsense. She just doesn't understand.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:37.900
Money for doctors doesn't come easy when you're a widow.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:43.733
Not unless you catch yourself some nice widower, like Mr. Mack next door.

00:02:43.733 --> 00:02:47.133
So you might just as well accept yourself the way you are.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.133
Forget the sports.

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:55.066
[Music]

00:02:55.066 --> 00:03:00.066
Which is it going to be, Kaye, the weak-woman bit or a doctor?

00:03:00.066 --> 00:03:25.866
[Dramatic music]

00:03:25.866 --> 00:03:28.432
[Kaye:] Hello, this is Kaye Riddle speaking.

00:03:28.433 --> 00:03:33.073
I want to make an appointment. I want to see Dr. Harris.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:39.760
[Music]

00:03:41.366 --> 00:03:43.532
[Narrator:] Name, Kaye Riddle.

00:03:43.533 --> 00:03:45.099
Sex, female.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.266
Age, 15.

00:03:47.266 --> 00:03:49.932
Primary symptom, fatigue.

00:03:49.933 --> 00:03:55.533
Diagnosis...well, let's see now.

00:03:55.533 --> 00:03:58.699
Oh, the report on the urinalysis.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:04.340
We better have the lab run a glucose-tolerance test on Kaye.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:12.800
Meanwhile though, well, it looks as if Kaye's had good reason to feel tired.

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:18.500
From her urinalysis and symptoms, there's a strong suspicion she has diabetes.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:21.566
Kaye is scared. So is her mother.

00:04:21.566 --> 00:04:25.132
Actually, diabetes is just a chronic disease.

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:29.266
Kaye's body doesn't break down sugars and fats efficiently.

00:04:29.266 --> 00:04:32.032
They aren't converted into energy.

00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:34.766
So, they collect in her system and make her sick.

00:04:34.766 --> 00:04:38.066
Uncontrolled, it's a pretty serious proposition.

00:04:38.066 --> 00:04:41.399
The whole idea still upsets Mrs. Riddle.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:45.866
Her grandmother and her Aunt Phoebe both died of diabetes.

00:04:45.866 --> 00:04:48.766
That sheds more light on Kaye's case.

00:04:48.766 --> 00:04:53.899
Diabetes is hereditary. It runs in families.

00:04:53.900 --> 00:05:02.000
But all Mrs. Riddle can think about is the trouble Grandma and Aunt Phoebe had with their starvation diets back when she was a girl.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.533
Of course, insulin takes care of all that now.

00:05:05.533 --> 00:05:11.466
But Mama just bears down on how Aunt Phoebe used to go into diabetic comas.

00:05:11.466 --> 00:05:19.066
Comas yet! There's no reason in the world for anyone to go into a diabetic coma these days, not with proper care.

00:05:19.066 --> 00:05:23.432
That's why it's so important to put Kaye under treatment right away,

00:05:23.433 --> 00:05:28.393
before she gets into real trouble, before complications develop.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:32.933
But try to get Mrs. Riddle to pay attention to a doctor.

00:05:32.933 --> 00:05:38.373
Like she keeps telling you, she's lived with diabetes, she knows.

00:05:39.966 --> 00:05:44.932
Trouble is, Mama Riddle knows so many things that just aren't so.

00:05:44.933 --> 00:05:48.866
Even worse, she does not know three facts.

00:05:48.866 --> 00:05:51.666
Key points, all of them.

00:05:51.666 --> 00:06:01.406
Fact one: diabetes is a disease like any other. A chronic disease you get when a gland called the pancreas doesn't work right.

00:06:04.266 --> 00:06:13.266
Fact two: diabetes can be controlled. Diabetics lead normal happy lives, once the disease is detected and properly treated.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:23.033
Fact three, control is fairly easy. Diet, exercise, insulin. That's all it takes.

00:06:23.033 --> 00:06:26.533
Kaye's a smart girl. So, she follows orders.

00:06:26.533 --> 00:06:31.013
Takes it for granted Dr. Harris knows what he's talking about.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:38.100
There's a daily test for sugar. It isn't difficult.

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:47.100
By one method, you simply dip a strip of special tape in urine, then match it to a color chart.

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:52.133
Other tests follow other procedures, but they all serve the same purpose.

00:06:52.133 --> 00:06:58.699
They help the diabetic to keep a constant check on his own condition.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:06.600
Mrs. Riddle tries to go along, though she does think this urine business is well, a little vulgar, maybe?

00:07:09.333 --> 00:07:14.633
Miss Wiley, the public health nurse, teaches Kaye how to inject insulin properly.

00:07:14.633 --> 00:07:18.933
The shots help make up for Kaye's pancreas not working right.

00:07:18.933 --> 00:07:22.393
And she finds they don't even hurt very much.

00:07:24.866 --> 00:07:29.106
To prevent infection, equipment must be sterilized.

00:07:29.106 --> 00:07:38.260
[Music]

00:07:38.266 --> 00:07:41.432
Continuing to follow the public health nurse's directions,

00:07:41.433 --> 00:07:46.273
Kaye loads the syringe with the correct type of insulin.

00:07:50.233 --> 00:07:53.233
Air is expelled.

00:07:53.233 --> 00:08:03.466
[Music]

00:08:03.466 --> 00:08:08.666
The skin is cleaned with alcohol.

00:08:08.666 --> 00:08:19.126
Kaye places the shot carefully, in order to reduce discomfort and avoid sores and scars.

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:29.033
Finally, she makes the injection. 
Good girl, Kaye.

00:08:29.033 --> 00:08:33.066
You're an apt pupil.

00:08:33.066 --> 00:08:38.386
The very thought of a needle gives Mrs. Riddle cold chills.

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:49.820
But Kaye figures Mama feels more real pain just plucking her eyebrows than anyone possibly could suffer from insulin injections.

00:08:52.033 --> 00:08:57.166
Another thing that bothers Mrs. Riddle is the way Kaye has to watch her diet.

00:08:57.166 --> 00:09:00.732
Poor girl, she has to deprive herself of so much.

00:09:00.733 --> 00:09:03.899
No more double-dip helpings of mashed potatoes.

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:07.533
No more ladles of thick brown gravy.

00:09:07.533 --> 00:09:09.999
No more rich cream sauces.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:13.900
No more drowning vegetables in butter.

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:17.666
Actually, Kaye doesn't like all such gooey glop.

00:09:17.666 --> 00:09:22.032
She doesn't feel as if she's starving, either.

00:09:22.033 --> 00:09:26.293
Breakfast? Kaye's certainly wasn't skimpy.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:31.433
Her luncheon didn't leave her weak.

00:09:31.433 --> 00:09:33.799
Dinner is satisfying too.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:37.466
And yes, Kaye can have mashed potatoes, within limits.

00:09:37.466 --> 00:09:41.732
Butter, biscuits, french dressing.

00:09:41.733 --> 00:09:45.433
Even luscious fresh fruits for dessert.

00:09:45.433 --> 00:09:53.899
But you can't convince Mama. She's sure Kaye is starving to death, and she eats twice as much herself to make up for it.

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:55.433
[Music]

00:09:55.433 --> 00:09:58.233
Between meals, even more so.

00:09:58.233 --> 00:10:03.966
It helps soothe her nerves when she gets to worrying over the cost of Kaye's diabetes.

00:10:03.966 --> 00:10:09.306
Why should the child have to keep running to the doctor and forever buying insulin?

00:10:11.666 --> 00:10:19.566
Of course, Mrs. Riddle's going to spend more money needlessly today on glassware than Kaye's medical expenses for a whole month.

00:10:19.566 --> 00:10:26.499
But Mama still wants Kaye to ask Dr. Harris if she has to come so often.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:29.766
But Kaye thinks health is worth a little money.

00:10:29.766 --> 00:10:32.466
She does what Dr. Harris tells her.

00:10:32.466 --> 00:10:35.146
Soon, her tests are negative.

00:10:37.066 --> 00:10:41.099
A diabetic out of control is thirsty all the time.

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:46.333
Before treatment, Kaye put a pitcher beside her bed every night.

00:10:46.333 --> 00:10:52.533
[Music]

00:10:52.533 --> 00:10:59.593
You drink a lot? Well, excessive urination is another major symptom of diabetes.

00:11:03.066 --> 00:11:08.832
[Toilet flushing]

00:11:08.833 --> 00:11:11.399
[Music]

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:17.700
But that's all past now. Kaye sleeps straight through.

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:22.966
Her weight goes up the way it should for a growing girl, diabetic or not.

00:11:22.966 --> 00:11:30.399
And once she's on target, all she has to do is hold her own.

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:37.633
Energy comes with control, and that shows up on a girl's report card.

00:11:37.633 --> 00:11:39.799
Kaye feels fine, too.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:47.300
Soon she's right back in the swim...with Eddie Roberts.

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:54.200
Miss Blake, the swimming instructor, notices how she's improving, and so does Miss Wiley, the public health nurse.

00:11:54.200 --> 00:12:00.733
[Music]

00:12:00.733 --> 00:12:05.166
There's even a compliment from Mr. Mack.

00:12:05.166 --> 00:12:12.599
Kaye learns that the country has nearly two million diabetics, and a million of them still don't know it.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:18.833
Mrs. Sorenson's case was detected when public health officials checked birth records.

00:12:18.833 --> 00:12:24.266
Mrs. Sorenson's oldest son weighed 11 pounds two ounces at birth.

00:12:24.266 --> 00:12:32.332
A child that heavy indicates to doctors that there may be diabetes in the family.

00:12:32.333 --> 00:12:39.899
At the County Health Department, a screening blood sugar estimation showed it was likely Mrs. Sorenson had diabetes.

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:46.833
So, she was referred to her family physician for diagnosis and treatment.

00:12:46.833 --> 00:12:55.066
Her doctor recommended that she attend a Health Department class for diabetics.

00:12:55.066 --> 00:13:00.326
Kaye soon learns that in the young, diabetes is a matter of life or death.

00:13:00.326 --> 00:13:05.433
If it isn't detected and controlled, the victim dies.

00:13:05.433 --> 00:13:10.499
In the older diabetic, the uncontrolled disease may bring complications.

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:17.266
Hardening of the arteries, blindness, gangrene, heart attacks, and strokes.

00:13:17.266 --> 00:13:24.732
Where Kaye's underweight, the older diabetic frequently is overweight, and because symptoms build up slowly,

00:13:24.733 --> 00:13:29.233
often the older diabetic doesn't even know that he's in trouble.

00:13:29.233 --> 00:13:33.199
That's why diabetes is so dangerous in the middle years.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:41.366
People just won't believe they have the disease 'til too late, after complications may have done damage that can't be repaired.

00:13:45.133 --> 00:13:47.399
Can diabetics have children?

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:53.666
Mrs. Campbell's healthy, happy family gives the answer to that question.

00:13:53.666 --> 00:13:59.732
Mrs. Lawson offers living proof that diabetics needn't die young.

00:13:59.733 --> 00:14:06.599
Mr. Groves built up a big, successful business.

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:09.366
Frank Hoover has a different kind of job.

00:14:09.366 --> 00:14:18.232
But even on the road all the time, doing heavy work and eating at restaurants, he still keeps his diabetes under control.

00:14:20.233 --> 00:14:26.166
It all helps Kaye to see how important prompt action and proper care are to a diabetic.

00:14:26.166 --> 00:14:34.299
When she suddenly feels weak while shopping, Kaye realizes that extra exercise has brought on a mild insulin reaction.

00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:39.966
So, she doesn't waste time, gets to a drugstore for a glass of orange juice.

00:14:39.966 --> 00:14:50.799
[Dramatic music]

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:54.780
Good work, Kaye. But what if you hadn't been near a drugstore?

00:14:54.820 --> 00:15:02.860
What if you'd passed out? Maybe it's time you filled out your diabetic identification card.

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:09.366
Carry hard candy to help counteract insulin reactions.

00:15:09.366 --> 00:15:15.332
Be sure to get the type of insulin prescribed.

00:15:15.333 --> 00:15:26.533
Diabetes affects circulation, so, to avoid gangrene, proper care of the feet is important.

00:15:26.533 --> 00:15:29.266
But Mama is Kaye's biggest problem.

00:15:29.266 --> 00:15:32.332
She likes being fat and happy, she says.

00:15:32.333 --> 00:15:36.133
She's not about to waste time on a check for diabetes.

00:15:36.133 --> 00:15:40.766
Heredity, familial tendencies, that's a lot of nonsense.

00:15:40.766 --> 00:15:47.566
What if Grandma did have diabetes, and Aunt Phoebe...Cousin Sam, too.

00:15:47.566 --> 00:15:48.766
Symptoms?

00:15:48.766 --> 00:15:54.132
Mama isn't bothered by excessive thirst and urination.

00:15:54.133 --> 00:15:56.933
She doesn't feel so well sometimes.

00:15:56.933 --> 00:16:03.033
To Mama, that's just the woman's weakness she claims runs in her family.

00:16:03.033 --> 00:16:08.733
Well, yes her weight is up, just a little.

00:16:08.733 --> 00:16:11.966
Is it any wonder?

00:16:11.966 --> 00:16:20.799
The fact is, in diabetics over 40, symptoms often don't show up clearly enough for the patient to recognize them.

00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:25.466
But Mama won't listen to such talk.

00:16:25.466 --> 00:16:33.466
No siree, that's not for mama, not while there's still syrup left in the pitcher.

00:16:33.466 --> 00:16:39.132
[Music]

00:16:39.133 --> 00:16:41.966
Kaye herself makes steady progress.

00:16:41.966 --> 00:16:46.632
There's even some slight chance she may not need to take insulin too long.

00:16:46.633 --> 00:16:52.199
Diet alone might hold the line, as it does for many older diabetics.

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:59.100
Kaye is reaching top form in the pool, too.

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:03.233
Miss Blake wants her to swim in the chorus at the water carnival.

00:17:03.233 --> 00:17:08.566
And Eddie Roberts himself is going to coach her.

00:17:08.566 --> 00:17:14.999
Later, when Eddie asks her for a date, well, the Riddle house is hardly big enough to hold her.

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:18.933
Only somehow that just seems to upset Mrs. Riddle.

00:17:18.933 --> 00:17:24.266
All she can think about is how her little girl is growing up.

00:17:24.266 --> 00:17:27.532
Well, Kaye's got her own ideas on that.

00:17:27.533 --> 00:17:33.233
Mr. Mack's sitting right next door, and could be that he and Mama...

00:17:33.233 --> 00:17:34.966
Kaye, that's ridiculous!

00:17:34.966 --> 00:17:40.499
Mr. Mack's never given Mama a second glance, that way.

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:47.333
Well, after all Mama, the way you look now, Mr. Mack probably figures he couldn't pay the grocery bills.

00:17:47.333 --> 00:17:51.333
Kaye, that wasn't the thing to say, really it wasn't.

00:17:51.333 --> 00:17:58.699
No, Kaye, no, you're only making it worse. Don't you dare tell your mother that no man wants to try to support an elephant these days,

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:05.533
especially not a sick elephant that maybe got uncontrolled diabetes.

00:18:05.533 --> 00:18:14.733
Now Mama, Kaye didn't mean anything. She loves you. She's just worried about your health.

00:18:14.733 --> 00:18:19.733
And besides, Mr. Mack really is a pretty nice fellow.

00:18:19.733 --> 00:18:51.099
[Music]

00:18:51.100 --> 00:19:00.000
[Mrs. Riddle:] This is Maude Riddle, Kaye's mother. I want to make an appointment with Dr. Harris.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.433
[Music]

00:19:01.433 --> 00:19:04.399
